IMPORT prelude

-- Environment Protection and Biodiversity Conservation Act 1999 (Cth), Parts 17 and 18 -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- Built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR), not the
-- daydate library. The only period these provisions count is "the 2 years immediately before" the conduct, the making
-- of the application, or the decision, failure or conduct (ss 475(6)(b), 475(7)(b), (c), 487(2)(b), (3)(b)).
--
-- Sourced from the Federal Register of Legislation, Commonwealth of Australia, CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the EPBC Act claims baseline of November 2026`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar day` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Whether the first day is strictly before the second.
GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first` `is earlier than` `the second` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` y IF
        y MODULO 4 EQUALS 0
    AND (    (NOT (y MODULO 100 EQUALS 0))
         OR  y MODULO 400 EQUALS 0)

GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` m y MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF m EQUALS 2 AND `is a leap year` y THEN 29
        IF m EQUALS 2 THEN 28
        IF m EQUALS 4 OR m EQUALS 6 OR m EQUALS 9 OR m EQUALS 11 THEN 30
        OTHERWISE 31

-- The same day of the month a number of whole years earlier. Where that year has no such day (29 February) it is the
-- last day of February (fork F2 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `the years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `minus calendar years` `the years` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY `the day of the month` (DATE_MONTH `the day`) `the year`
    WHERE
        `the year` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the day` MINUS `the years`
        `the last day` MEANS `the days in month` (DATE_MONTH `the day`) `the year`
        `the day of the month` MEANS IF DATE_DAY `the day` GREATER THAN `the last day` THEN `the last day` ELSE DATE_DAY `the day`

-- The first day of "the 2 years immediately before" a day: the same day of the month 2 years earlier (fork F1).
GIVEN `the end day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day of the 2 years before` `the end day` MEANS `the end day` `minus calendar years` 2

-- Whether an activity on a day was "at any time in the 2 years immediately before" the end day: on or after the first
-- day of the 2 years, and on or before the end day itself (fork F1: an activity on the very day counts).
GIVEN `the activity day` IS A DATE, `the end day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity day` `falls in the 2 years immediately before` `the end day` IF
        (NOT (`the activity day` `is earlier than` (`the first day of the 2 years before` `the end day`)))
    AND (NOT (`the end day` `is earlier than` `the activity day`))
